# Premises for rent in Russian: located, renovated, built
subtitle: "Помеще́ние, располо́женное во́зле метро́: read and turn round Russian past passive participles, as Tom looks at premises for his restaurant."
tags: ["russian","passive participles","russian participles","renting in russian","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/participles","vocabulary/business"]
thumb: "band \"Read a Russian listing\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
